      "message": "Could we implement that in a non-intrusive way using instrumentation of our compiler ?\n\nUsing something like `-finstrument-functions`\n\n```\n#define _GNU_SOURCE\n#include \u003cstdio.h\u003e\n#include \u003clink.h\u003e\n#include \u003cdlfcn.h\u003e\n\n\n__attribute__((no_instrument_function))\nvoid __cyg_profile_func_enter(void *this_fn, void *call_site) {\n  Dl_info info \u003d {0,};\n\n  dladdr(this_fn, \u0026info);\n\n  printf(\"enter: %s(%p), from %p\\n\", info.dli_sname, this_fn, call_site);\n}\n\n__attribute__((no_instrument_function))\nvoid __cyg_profile_func_exit(void *this_fn, void *call_site) {\n}\n\nvoid hello() {\n}\n\nint main(int argc, char** argv) {\n  hello();\n  return 0;\n}\n```\n\n```\n$ gcc -finstrument-functions test.c -ldl -rdynamic\n$ ./a.out\nenter: main(0x55cef307a1e0), from 0x7fded8efe18a\nenter: hello(0x55cef307a1ad), from 0x55cef307a210\n```",
